# Sweet Potato and Black Bean Quinoa Bowls

Based on [https://www.spoonfulofflavor.com/sweet-potato-black-bean-quinoa-bowls/…](https://www.spoonfulofflavor.com/sweet-potato-black-bean-quinoa-bowls/) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251125114813/https://www.spoonfulofflavor.com/sweet-potato-black-bean-quinoa-bowls/))

{ rating="4" image="sweet_potato_and_black_bean_quinoa_bowls.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Roasted Sweet Potato:

- [ ] 1 large [sweet potato]{ ing="sweet-potato" }, peeled and diced
- [ ] 1 tsp extra [virgin olive oil]{ ing="virgin-olive-oil" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [cumin]{ ing="cumin" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }

### Cilantro Cream Drizzle:

- [ ] 1/4 cup plain non [fat Greek yogurt]{ ing="fat-greek-yogurt" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, chopped
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [agave nectar]{ ing="agave-nectar" } or honey
- [ ] Juice of half a [lime]{ ing="lime" }
- [ ] Pinch of [salt]{ ing="salt" }, garlic powder, and chili powder

### Quinoa:

- [ ] 1.5 cups [red quinoa]{ ing="red-quinoa" }
- [ ] 3 cups [water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, divided
- [ ] 1 tsp [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [cumin]{ ing="cumin" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
- [ ] Juice of [half a lime]{ ing="lime" }
- [ ] 3 Tbsp [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, chopped

### Other Ingredients:

- [ ] 1 cup [black beans]{ ing="black-beans" }, rinsed and drained
- [ ] [Cilantro for garnishing]{ ing="cilantro-for-garnishing" }

## Recipe

1. Start the [quinoa]{ ing="red-quinoa" } in a rice cooker
1. Roast the [Sweet Potato]{ ing="sweet-potato" }:

   1. Preheat oven to 425F. Prepare a large baking sheet with a baking mat, foil, or cooking spray
   1. Toss the diced sweet potato in the [olive oil]{ ing="virgin-olive-oil" } and spices. Spread out in an even layer on the baking sheet
   1. Roast the sweet potato for 12-15 minutes or until it is fork tender
1. For the [Cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" } Cream Drizzle, in a blender, add all of the ingredients and blend until smooth

   1. _Easier sauce alternatives:_ Plain [Greek yogurt]{ ing="fat-greek-yogurt" } with [lime]{ ing="lime" } juice, store-bought cilantro lime dressing, or simply drizzle with lime juice and olive oil
1. Once the quinoa is done, season with the specified spices
1. Assembling the Bowls:

   1. In 2 or 3 serving bowls divide the quinoa mixture
   1. Top the quinoa with the [black beans]{ ing="black-beans" } and roasted sweet potato
   1. Drizzle the cilantro cream on top with a spoon. Top with more cilantro if desired.
